build: 2026-06-30 v10.76.50 (Menu-freeze ROOT CAUSE found + camera fps-collapse fix)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: The recurring "kann während Biofeedback nicht mehr in den Dropdowns auswählen" —
  finally the ACTUAL cause, one level above where I'd been looking.
  • ROOT CAUSE (menu freeze): the persistent top bar (WorkspaceView.topBar — it sits ABOVE
    every surface) read the live pulse waveform/BPM directly to feed the little header pulse
    monitor. The waveform updates ~10×/s while biofeedback runs, so WorkspaceView — the PARENT
    of the whole instrument — rebuilt 10×/s, and every rebuild tore down any open dropdown in
    the surface below it (Compose/Mood/Effects). Earlier fixes all checked the instrument view
    (EchoelStudioView) and correctly found it clean — but the churn was in the ROOT above it,
    so it was never seen. FIX: the live reads now live inside the small monitor leaf
    (PulseMonitorMiniLive); WorkspaceView no longer subscribes to the 10 Hz signal, so the
    surface tree (and your open menus) stays still while bio runs. This is the real fix.
  • CAMERA fps-collapse (from your pasted log): the first lock worked (≈54 bpm), but after you
    lifted/replaced the finger the camera frame rate fell to ~3 fps (log: rate 15→4.8→3.1) and
    the pulse could never re-lock. Cause: exposure lock used plain ".locked", which freezes
    whatever long exposure the dim fingertip scene last chose — a long exposure forces a low
    frame rate. FIX: lock with a bounded custom exposure (≤1/30 s) so the frame rate can't drop
    below ~30 fps (and it saturates less). Reacquisition should now re-lock instead of stalling
    at rate≈3.
  Build-checked. Test: 10.76.50 → start the camera pulse, then open Compose ▸ Composition ▸
  Genre/Tonart (and Mood, Effects) and change them repeatedly WHILE measuring — they must stay
  open and selectable. Lift + replace your finger → it should re-lock (no rate≈3 stall). If a
  dropdown STILL freezes, tell me — but this was the measured parent-rebuild cause.
